course: dictionary
lesson: 16025
title: Venerate: showing deep respect
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Venerate is a formal verb. To venerate someone or something is to treat them with very deep respect. Look at the clues around it. «The villagers venerated the wise old woman who had taught them to farm.» The words wise and taught tell you she was admired and respected, so venerated means greatly respected.
explain: Some words give strong clues. «Many Christians venerate saints, honouring them as holy people.» Honouring is a clue: to venerate is to honour. In church, venerating a saint, a relic or an icon means you honour it with great respect, but you believe only God is worshipped.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The children venerate their grandparents» becomes «The children greatly respect their grandparents», and it still makes sense. You can also find the noun veneration, which is the act of showing that deep respect.
fact: Venerate means to treat someone or something with very deep respect.
fact: «The villagers venerated the wise old woman.» Here it means greatly respected.
fact: In church, Christians may venerate saints, relics or icons: they honour them, but only God is worshipped.
fact: Venerate is a verb: venerates, venerated, venerating. The noun is veneration.
fact: Venerate is a formal word, used in religion, history and serious writing.
exercise: «Many people venerate their grandparents as the wisest members of the family.» What does venerate mean here? | Argue with politely | Forget quickly | *Treat with deep respect | Ignore on purpose
exercise: Some Christians venerate saints. Do they believe saints are worshipped like God? | Yes, saints are worshipped only on Sundays | Yes, they worship saints as they worship God | No, they never honour saints at all | *No, they honour saints, but believe only God is worshipped
exercise: Which word is the noun form of venerate, meaning the act of showing deep respect? | *veneration | venerated | venerates | venerating
test: «The villagers venerated the wise old woman who had healed them.» What does venerated mean in that sentence? | Insulted | Laughed at | Forgotten | *Greatly respected
test: Which word is closest in meaning to venerate? | *Honour | Mock | Ignore | Despise
exam: Why might a church venerate an icon but not worship it? | *Because it honours the icon, while only God is worshipped | Because the icon is made of gold | Because it sells the icon | Because the icon is alive
